{"disableMarkdown": false, "noteFontSize": 14, "pages": [{"idx": 2, "label": "3", "note": "- three parts, about ten minutes each\n- leave time for questions at the end", "overlay": 0}, {"idx": 4, "label": "4", "note": "- terracotta: heavier, it **breathes** and dries faster\n- plastic: cheap, ask who already uses it", "overlay": 0}, {"idx": 6, "label": "5", "note": "- the mix is 3 parts of soil and 1 of sand\n- compost\\_mix in the shop is the same thing, only more expensive\n- *never* garden soil: it gets hard in pots", "overlay": 0}, {"idx": 9, "label": "6", "note": "- check the balcony orientation first\n- south and west: tomatoes; north: herbs\\* and lettuce", "overlay": 0}, {"idx": 11, "label": "7", "note": "1. basil indoors, near a window\n2. lettuce outside, a short row every three weeks", "overlay": 0}, {"idx": 13, "label": "8", "note": "- in July twice a day\n- a saucer under the pot keeps a reserve of water", "overlay": 0}, {"idx": 15, "label": "9", "note": "> pick young, pick often\n\n- tomatoes ripen indoors too, out of the sun", "overlay": 0}], "pdfpcFormat": 2}